• Result: This instantly terminates their background Node.js processes, freeing up massive amounts of uncompressed physical memory.

2. Clean Up Your Settings Configuration

You need to explicitly command the editor to stop spending CPU cycles on telemetry, background scanning, and file updates. Open your settings file (Ctrl + ,, click the code icon in the top right to view the raw JSON), and add these precise lines to freeze background activity:
json
"telemetry.telemetryLevel": "off",
"git.autorefresh": false,
"git.autofetch": false,
"extensions.autoCheckUpdates": false,
"extensions.autoUpdate": false,
"workbench.startPage.showWeeklyTips": false
Use code with caution.

