3. Why This Specific Route Keeps Your Machine Flying

By choosing this split-lane design, you solve the biggest issue with running automated AIs on local 4GB physical hardware: thread locking.
1. Cursorless and Ingestion stay in the fast lane: Since Unit 1 and Unit 3 are just handling text ingestion, they consume almost zero CPU power and run entirely in your uncompressed 4GB physical RAM. When you use your voice to target a block of code, your microphone inputs and Cursorless token updates register instantly without lag.
2. Heavy math stays in the background cache: The massive computational work of processing neural weights happens entirely inside Unit 2 and Unit 4. Because these models sit compressed inside your 12GB ZSTD zram space, they crunch numbers without hogging the active foreground lanes.
You get the true performance of a multi-agent framework running off the top, entirely offline, twice as fast, with zero wasted output.
