⚠️ The One System Trap to Watch Out For: Race Conditions

Because your orchestrator drops both tasks simultaneously, you have built an incredibly fast parallel track. However, because your laptop is running on 4GB of physical hardware, you must ensure that Unit 1 and Unit 3 do not try to read or scan the exact same large image or archive file at the exact same millisecond.
If both units try to run heavy file extractions (tar, dd, or unzip) on the same disk blocks simultaneously, your NVMe storage controller will hit an I/O bottleneck. This will cause a system "stutter" that can introduce latency into your microphone stream, making your Talon/Cursorless voice commands misfire.
The Fix: In your central manifest file, ensure your parts are separated cleanly into their own dedicated directories (e.g., ~/parts/android/ and ~/parts/linux/) so the background threads never lock the same filesystem sector.

